{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-crossroads-continent/1546135-inktober-postings-and-story-with-art-redux-5","id":1546135,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Crossroads Continent"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-19T10:27:56-08:00","id":1546135,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #5","content":"Inktober Redux5: The trading post is called Greenclaw's or T'Shar's Pillar and is named for the current leader of the inhabitants, who came to a much less thriving trading post with his albino sister and has rejuvenated it. Both of the lizardmen seem to have contact with their tribe, as well as other lizardman tribes, so what prompted T'Shar to settle at the post is something only the two of them know.<br /> <br /> Antoine Ce'Lantro actually pre-dates the Greenclaws as he once used the site as a rest stop during his decades as a pirate out in the sea and around the Whalebone Islands. Of course, now he owns and frequents the Grog &amp; Grog saloon, and enjoys reliving his glory days with the other patrons. His keen knowledge of both battle strategy and human(oid) nature is appreciated by the town council, led by T'Shar. Quack-yaaar!<br /> <br /> The rest of the inhabitants of Greenclaw's Pillar are a mix of traders, merchants, and mercenaries, who make their livings off of those who come to the post, archeologists and adventurers who explore the ancient ruins buried under the plant life, and a few folks hiding out in this very small outpost buried under the canopy of the Algernon Forest lowlands and swamps. Some have relatively decent motives, and others the darkest, but in general, they cooperate under the watchful eyes of the Greenclaw siblings. Alliances come together and shift, but a bite out of your arm by S'Shar is always painful.<br /> <br /> Speaking of taking bites, there's Malcolm. He joined the crew of the M'udd pirates 